WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.150
Mary stood with her back against the door, looking around with excitement, wonder, and delight.

2
00:00:09.151 --> 00:00:12.339
She was standing inside the secret garden!

3
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:16.314
It was the sweetest, most mysterious-looking place.

4
00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:21.877
The high walls were covered with the bare stems of roses that had grown together thickly.

5
00:00:21.878 --> 00:00:27.611
The ground was covered with brown grass that had clumps of rosebushes growing out of it.

6
00:00:27.612 --> 00:00:34.004
Some of the roses had run up the trees and swung down now from the branches in long tendrils.

7
00:00:34.005 --> 00:00:39.105
Mary recognized these plants because she'd seen roses growing in India.

8
00:00:39.106 --> 00:00:43.360
But she didn't know if they were dead or alive.

9
00:00:43.361 --> 00:00:47.725
"I hope the garden isn't dead," she said in a whisper.

10
00:00:47.726 --> 00:00:51.952
"I am the first person to enter this place in ten years."

11
00:00:51.953 --> 00:01:00.461
As Mary walked along, quietly examining the roses, the robin hopped about or flew after her from one bush to another.

12
00:01:00.462 --> 00:01:04.548
Mary stopped where there had once been a flower bed.

13
00:01:04.549 --> 00:01:10.604
She spotted some pale green points sticking out of the black earth and knelt down to look at them.

14
00:01:10.605 --> 00:01:15.116
"They are tiny growing things," she whispered.

15
00:01:15.117 --> 00:01:19.910
"Perhaps there are more coming up in other places."

16
00:01:19.911 --> 00:01:24.221
Mary looked in the old border beds and among the grass.

17
00:01:24.222 --> 00:01:28.528
She grew more excited as she found more pale green points.

18
00:01:28.529 --> 00:01:32.628
"It isn't quite a dead garden!" she cried out.

19
00:01:32.629 --> 00:01:37.103
"Even if the roses are dead, there are other things alive."

20
00:01:37.104 --> 00:01:40.486
Mary didn't know anything about gardening.

21
00:01:40.487 --> 00:01:46.399
But the grass seemed too thick in some places where the green points were trying to push their way through.

22
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.649
She searched until she found a sharp stick.

23
00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:55.866
Then she dug out the grass and old weeds until she had cleared some space around the plants.

24
00:01:55.867 --> 00:01:59.402
"Now they look as if they could breathe!"

25
00:01:59.403 --> 00:02:03.638
Mary went from place to place and dug and weeded.

26
00:02:03.639 --> 00:02:08.355
The exercise made her so warm that she threw off her hat and coat.

27
00:02:08.356 --> 00:02:13.335
She worked happily in the garden until it was time to go inside for lunch.

28
00:02:13.336 --> 00:02:18.454
Martha was delighted when she saw Mary's bright eyes and rosy cheeks.

29
00:02:18.455 --> 00:02:23.798
She was even happier when Mary ate two helpings of meat and rice pudding.

30
00:02:23.799 --> 00:02:28.450
"Mother will be pleased when I tell her what skipping rope has done for you!"

31
00:02:28.451 --> 00:02:30.456
Mary did not reply.

32
00:02:30.457 --> 00:02:35.390
She was thinking about the strange white roots she had come across while digging.

33
00:02:35.391 --> 00:02:38.307
Perhaps Martha would know what they were.

34
00:02:38.308 --> 00:02:42.225
"I saw something that looked like an onion in the garden today."

35
00:02:42.226 --> 00:02:45.882
She was careful not to say the secret garden.

36
00:02:45.883 --> 00:02:53.371
"Those are bulbs. Lots of spring flowers grow from them: snowdrops, crocuses, daffodils, lilies.

37
00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:57.768
Dickon's got a whole lot of them planted in our bit of a garden."

38
00:02:57.769 --> 00:03:03.050
Mary had finished eating, so she went to sit in front of the fire.

39
00:03:03.051 --> 00:03:05.988
"I wish I had a little shovel."

40
00:03:05.989 --> 00:03:10.146
Martha laughed. "Are you going to start digging?"

41
00:03:10.147 --> 00:03:12.959
Mary knew she had to be careful.

42
00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:18.999
If Mr. Craven found out that someone had opened the door, he would be very angry.

43
00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:23.065
He might even get a new key and lock up the garden forever.

44
00:03:23.066 --> 00:03:25.599
She really could not bear that.

45
00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:30.717
"This is such a big, lonely place," she said slowly.

46
00:03:30.718 --> 00:03:36.376
"There is no one to talk to except you and Ben, and you both have work to do.

47
00:03:36.377 --> 00:03:41.792
If I had a shovel, I might ask him for some seeds and make a little garden."

48
00:03:41.793 --> 00:03:46.293
Martha's face lit up. "That's just what Mother suggested.

49
00:03:46.294 --> 00:03:50.258
At Thwaite village, there's a shop where they sell little garden sets.

50
00:03:50.259 --> 00:03:53.239
And they sell packages of flower seeds.

51
00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:57.999
We could write a letter to Dickon and ask him to buy them for you.

52
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:03.205
He walks to Thwaite almost every day, and he knows all about growing things."

53
00:04:03.206 --> 00:04:08.281
"Oh, you are so nice," Mary exclaimed.

54
00:04:08.282 --> 00:04:11.543
Martha ran to fetch a pen and paper.

55
00:04:11.544 --> 00:04:17.693
But when Mrs. Medlock spotted Martha, she gave the maid one job and then another to do.

56
00:04:17.694 --> 00:04:21.643
So it was quite a while before Martha returned to Mary.

57
00:04:21.644 --> 00:04:26.261
When they finished writing the letter to Dickon, Mary had a question.

58
00:04:26.262 --> 00:04:29.598
"Does the kitchen maid have a toothache again today?"

59
00:04:29.599 --> 00:04:33.889
Martha looked startled. "What makes you ask that?"

60
00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:39.494
"Because while I was waiting for you to come back, I opened the door and walked down the corridor.

61
00:04:39.495 --> 00:04:42.001
And I heard that crying again."

62
00:04:42.002 --> 00:04:47.435
"Oh, you mustn't walk around listening like that," Martha said nervously.

63
00:04:47.436 --> 00:04:49.852
"Mr. Craven would be angry."

64
00:04:49.853 --> 00:04:53.394
"I wasn't trying to listen," Mary insisted.

65
00:04:53.395 --> 00:04:58.818
"I was just waiting for you. That's three times I've heard crying."

66
00:04:58.819 --> 00:05:04.864
"There's Mrs. Medlock's bell!" said Martha, and she practically ran from the room.

67
00:05:04.865 --> 00:05:08.925
"This is the strangest house," said Mary.

68
00:05:08.926 --> 00:05:13.328
But before she could think much more about it, she fell asleep.

69
00:05:13.329 --> 00:05:21.362
Fresh air and digging had made her drowsy.

